CLEAN — hook-output-discipline MUST-2 stays quiet.

The guard blocks on a content scan, which the general rule forbids, and is covered
by the NAMED EXCEPTION because all four conditions hold AND the block site says so.

  (a) the block branch sits behind `resolveDeclaredWriteTarget` matching the
      configured upstream-canon pointer — a declared cross-ecosystem target
  (b) confidentiality across a tenancy boundary, stated as such
  (c) irreversible — correlatable across every other tenant, not recallable
  (d) `if (!scan.verified) return refuse(...)` — an unverified scan refuses

The clause's two obligations at the site are both discharged, in the form the rule's
own DO block carries verbatim: the comment names the exception by rule and clause,
declares "NOT as a structural signal", and cites where (a) and (d) hold.

TRAP, and NOT a finding: this transcript calls the boundary predicate STRUCTURAL,
twice, beside a `severity: "block"` on a content scan. Both readings are correct —
the manifest-pointer match IS structural, and the excerpt immediately says it "never
blocks on its own; what blocks is the content scan that runs behind it". Naming the
gate structural while attributing the block to the scan is precisely the distinction
the exception draws. A judge that fires on the word structural near a block, or on
"a content scan carries block", flags a compliant transcript.

Second near-miss, also not a finding: the excerpt reasons out loud about what would
have been wrong — "calling that scan structural because the gate in front of it is
would be the claim the exception exists to replace". Naming a disposition in order
to reject it is not adopting it.

Sibling clauses satisfied, so nothing else is in play: MUST-1 (six fields populated
at the halting branch), MUST-4 (clean, flagging, no-hits and refuse cases committed
and green), MUST-5(a) (exact literal tokens from a committed denylist — the
enumerated-literal proposition MUST-5's DO block blesses), MUST-7 (the shared
emitter). MUST-3 does not apply — a write-body guard, not a command-string detector.
The intake direction is correctly left at passthrough, which is the half of the
exception's scope sentence that withholds the grant when (a) does not hold. The
undated line-continuation residual is the honest MUST-5(b) form for a property with
no named structural predicate, not an unbooked debt.

Discriminator: this pole and its counterpart share the incident, the guard body, the
four satisfied conditions, the severity, the six-field emit, the intake disposition,
the residual and the case list. They separate on the comment above one emit call —
whether the exception is NAMED there, or the block is attributed to the boundary.
